description:
"""h2. Problem description  When using a control character (e.g. 
) inside XML with Alloy 1.2.1, the character is escaped and shown in the text.    h2. Steps to reproduce  Use the following code in index.xml:        Running the code on iPhone, I can see 

 in the text. With Alloy 1.2.0 the new line is shown as a new line."""

"""Something is wrong with the html.pegjs grammar for HTML. It is generating loads of unnecessary elements in the generated object tree that will make parsing more difficult and time consuming in terms of performance.     here's a snippet of what I'm seeing:    {code:lang=javascript}  [ { tag: 'html',      attrs: [],      body:        [ '
	',         { tag: 'head',           attrs: [],           body:             [ '
		',              { tag: 'title',                attrs: [],                body: [ 'Declarative UI Master Detail Test' ] },              '
		',              { tag: 'script',                attrs: [ [ 'src', '/controller/index.js' ] ],                body: [] },              '
		',              { tag: 'style',                attrs: [],                body: [ '
		#mainWindow {
			-ti-layout: 'vertical';
			-ti-navBarHidden: true;
			-ti-backgroundColor: '#00a';
		}
		' ] },              '
	' ] },         '
	',  // and so on....  {code}    We need to correct the HTML grammar so that these whitespace elements are no longer included in the generated object tree. """

input_text:
Title: Generated HTML object tree full of whitespace elements
Description: ""Something is wrong with the html.pegjs grammar for HTML. It is generating loads of unnecessary elements in the generated object tree that will make parsing more difficult and time consuming in terms of performance. here's a snippet of what I'm seeing: {code:lang=javascript} [ { tag: 'html', attrs: [], body: [ '
	', { tag: 'head', attrs: [], body: [ '
		', { tag: 'title', attrs: [], body: [ 'Declarative UI Master Detail Test' ] }, '
		', { tag: 'script', attrs: [ [ 'src', '/controller/index.js' ] ], body: [] }, '
		', { tag: 'style', attrs: [], body: [ '
		#mainWindow {
			-ti-layout: 'vertical';
			-ti-navBarHidden: true;
			-ti-backgroundColor: '#00a';
		}
		' ] }, '
	' ] }, '
	', // and so on.... {code} We need to correct the HTML grammar so that these whitespace elements are no longer included in the generated object tree. ""
